<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso IX of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1171–1230</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso IX was king of León from 1188 to 1230. In his first year he summoned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> of León, which included townsmen alongside nobles and clergy and is often cited as the earliest European parliament of its kind. He took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caceres">Cáceres</a>, Mérida and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>, and his son Ferdinand III united León and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-ix-of-leon.jpg" alt="Alfonso IX of León" width="320" height="566" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adeffonsus,_king_of_Galicia_and_Leon_(detail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
